& [Threats]
  + [T01] PATH or desktop substitution is refused by exact absolute native path hash file identity and signer replay
  + [T02] preexisting-envelope destruction is refused because creation requires observed absence and no cleanup authority exists
  + [T03] repository overlap is refused by fixed cross-volume root relations and canonical identity checks
  + [T04] inherited credentials proxies helpers or state are refused by env_clear-first launch and closed nonsecret additions
  + [T05] provider contact is refused by schema-generation-only argv no thread turn MCP model browser connector WebSocket or network surface
  + [T06] shell injection is refused by direct executable and fixed argument-vector launch
  + [T07] unbounded output or hang is refused by concurrent bounded drains deadline owned-child termination wait and late-output accounting
  + [T08] descendant escape is refused unless every observed descendant is terminal; ambiguity quarantines the fixture
  + [T09] schema output escape is refused by exact schema root post-state inventory and out-of-root change detection
  + [T10] ambient Git identity or hooks are refused by exact git executable fixed config environment and no remote
  + [T11] false final-B1 promotion is refused because preparation and schema success close no sandbox canary or preflight evidence requirement
  + [T12] evidence self-production is refused because final B1 producer verifier and recovery duties remain separate
  + [T13] retry substitution is refused; drift or unsupported selected binary becomes a terminal preparation refusal
  + [T14] foreign-work capture is refused by explicit path attribution and staged-path allowlisting

& [Residual]
  + successful schema generation does not prove App Server initialize command/exec sandbox or read-only behavior
  + Windows process descendant enumeration strength and exact minimal environment remain empirical inputs to the final lock
  + fixture is intentionally retained under recovery ownership after any preparation attempt

& [Decision]
  + threats are bounded for one preparation attempt
  + no authority exists for cleanup or a final B1 launch under this review
